pppd: clear pppdb after tdb_close() in ppp_safe_fork()

Backport of the ppp-project/ppp upstream fix (2026-09-28, "pppd: Clear pppdb
after tdb_close() in ppp_safe_fork()"). run_program() calls
ppp_script_setenv("PPP_SCRIPT_INSTANCE") in the forked child, which still sees
the dangling pppdb and calls tdb_store() on freed memory: the child segfaults
before exec, so ip-up/ip-down never run and PPPoE redials forever. Only builds
with PPP_WITH_TDB (multilink) are affected. Log signature:
"SIOCGIFFLAGS: Bad file descriptor", then "Fatal signal 11".

diff --git a/release/src-rt-6.x.4708/router/pppd/pppd/main.c b/release/src-rt-6.x.4708/router/pppd/pppd/main.c
index fecf9a038..d9e3abea3 100644
--- a/release/src-rt-6.x.4708/router/pppd/pppd/main.c
+++ b/release/src-rt-6.x.4708/router/pppd/pppd/main.c
@@ -1726,8 +1726,10 @@ ppp_safe_fork(int infd, int outfd, int errfd)
 	/* Executing in the child */
 	ppp_sys_close();
 #ifdef PPP_WITH_TDB
-	if (pppdb != NULL)
+	if (pppdb != NULL) {
 		tdb_close(pppdb);
+		pppdb = NULL;	/* tdb_close() can't null the caller's pointer */
+	}
 #endif
 
 	/* make sure infd, outfd and errfd won't get tromped on below */
